@startuml Zemen_EventLifecycle
!pragma layout smetana
title Zemen — Event Lifecycle State Diagram

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #333333
  FontName Arial
  ArrowColor #555555
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #F9A825
  FontName Arial
}

[*] --> Persisted : Owner calls POST /events\n(single or recurring series)

state Persisted {
  [*] --> Draft : event inserted\nversion = 1\nsnapshot saved
  Draft : start_time_utc > now
  Draft : reminder not yet sent
}

Persisted --> Ongoing : start_time_utc <= now\n(time-based transition,\nNOT stored in DB)

state Ongoing {
  [*] --> Running : event in progress
  Running : start_time_utc <= now
  Running : end_time_utc > now (or NULL)
  Running : reminder already sent\n(if SMTP configured)
}

Ongoing --> Past : end_time_utc <= now\n(only if end_time_utc is NOT NULL;\nevents with NULL end_time_utc\nremain Ongoing indefinitely)

state Past {
  [*] --> Ended
  Ended : end_time_utc < now
  Ended : snapshots retained for audit
  Ended : visible on calendar as\npast event
}

Persisted --> Deleted : Owner calls\nDELETE /events/{id}
Ongoing --> Deleted  : Owner calls\nDELETE /events/{id}
Past --> Deleted     : Owner calls\nDELETE /events/{id}

Deleted --> [*]

note right of Persisted
  Created by POST /events.
  version = 1, snapshot saved immediately.
  Reminder scheduled: fires at
  start_time_utc − reminder_minutes
  (reminder_minutes default = 60).
  Participants can be added via
  POST /events/{id}/share.
end note

note right of Ongoing
  Event is in progress.
  Edits (PUT /events/{id}) still allowed
  by owner or editor — version increments,
  new snapshot saved after each edit.
  Optimistic locking (version check) active.
end note

note right of Past
  end_time_utc has passed.
  Snapshots and participants are retained.
  Diff (GET /events/{id}/diff) still available.
  Hard DELETE still possible — removes event,
  snapshots, and participants (CASCADE).
end note

note right of Deleted
  Hard DELETE from PostgreSQL.
  ON DELETE CASCADE removes:
    event_snapshots, event_participants,
    reminder_logs linked to this event.
  No soft-delete or archive; data is gone.
end note

note bottom
  **Implementation facts:**
  • Event model has NO status column — states are temporal (derived from datetime comparisons).
  • delete_event() in events.py is unconditional — requires only owner role, not any particular "state."
  • Events with NULL end_time_utc never enter Past state.
  • Recurrence series: multiple Event rows share recurrence_group_id (UUID).
    DELETE /events/{id}/series with scope="all"|"from_here" removes the group.
end note

@enduml
